# MCP server bundle (built by `npm run mcp:build`)
dist-mcp/

# The cover pipeline's working directories: review dumps, rejects, installers and caches. The *shipped* artwork is
# `public/covers/<genre>.jpg` and `public/covers/<skin>/<genre>.jpg`; none of these are loaded by the app.
public/covers/_installed/
public/covers/_rejected/
public/covers/_review/
public/covers/_batch_scratch/
public/covers/__pycache__/
public/covers/_thumbs/
public/covers/_batch_*

# The per-skin genre artwork is a **deploy-time asset drop**, not source: six skins of 159 JPEGs is ~200 MB, which belongs
# next to the build that copies `public/` into `dist/`, not in the repository. `src/test/genreCovers.test.ts` states the
# contract: a skin whose directory is absent is skipped (this checkout has no drop), while one that is present must be
# complete. The shared `public/covers/<genre>.jpg` set *is* tracked, because it is what every skin falls back to.
public/covers/default/
public/covers/minimal/
public/covers/comic/
public/covers/soviet/
public/covers/sovietYears/
public/covers/pixel/

tools/covers/__pycache__/
tools/covers/_batch_scratch/
public/covers/_*
